From c74a6aa5f650e26907703832d04ba4a3c7899dfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 02:56:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] perf(clangd): qualified completion loads matching external
 names

External namespace completion previously materialized every declaration before
fuzzy matching. Pass a synchronous consumer predicate to the external source
and select identifier keys before declaration deserialization. Preserve complete
ordinary lookup, all overload IDs and nonidentifier traversal names; keep
external storage for omitted names. The consumer defaults to complete loading.

Tests exercise real precompiled headers and named modules, fuzzy/empty queries,
using and inline namespaces, aliases and hiding, merged/overriding lookup tables,
ordinary lookup after selection, and synchronous source/context scope cleanup.
